  🚀 HIGH PRIORITY - Protocol Support

  4. PMBus Protocol Layer

  Status: Mentioned in future plans but not implemented
  Enhancement: Complete PMBus implementation over SMBus
  - All PMBus commands (voltage, current, temperature monitoring)
  - Linear11/Linear16 data format handling
  - Power supply management
  - Fault monitoring

  Use Cases:
  - Power supply monitoring and control
  - Server power management
  - Battery management systems

  5. I3C Protocol Support

  Enhancement: Add I3C (Improved Inter-Integrated Circuit)
  - Backward compatible with I2C
  - Higher speeds (12.5 MHz typical, up to 33 MHz)
  - In-band interrupts
  - Hot-join capability
  - Dynamic address assignment

  Benefits:
  - Future-proof for modern sensors
  - Better performance than I2C
  - Fewer pins than SPI with similar speeds

  6. 1-Wire Interface

  Enhancement: Dallas/Maxim 1-Wire protocol
  - Temperature sensors (DS18B20)
  - EEPROM devices
  - iButton authentication

  Benefits:
  - Single-wire communication
  - Parasitic power option
  - Common for temperature sensing

  7. UART/Serial Bus Support

  Enhancement: Add UART as managed bus type
  - RS-232, RS-485 support
  - Modbus RTU/ASCII protocol
  - Unified interface with other buses

  Use Cases:
  - Industrial communication
  - GPS modules
  - Bluetooth/WiFi modules

